From 3d1db2c8684c5df2db6a0f9297f3749612876951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 20:08:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3 Plan B re-verify: silicon-OK confirmed at addr 0x20+
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Modified mode_epcs_probe Phase E to read addr 0x20..0x2F instead of
0..3, motivated by EPCS dump revealing flash bytes 0..0x1F are all
0xff (factory ALINX bitstream header padding).

HW result: 16/16 byte-IDENTICAL match between Plan B v3 silicon reads
and EPCS backup dump:
  addr  Plan B  Backup
  0x20  0x56    0x56
  0x21  0xef    0xef
  0x22  0xef    0xef
  0x23  0xef    0xef
  0x24  0xef    0xef
  0x25  0xef    0xef
  0x26  0xef    0xef
  0x27  0xcf    0xcf
  0x28  0xdf    0xdf
  0x29  0xdf    0xdf
  0x2a  0x9f    0x9f
  0x2b  0xdf    0xdf
  0x2c  0x9f    0x9f
  0x2d  0x8f    0x8f
  0x2e  0x9f    0x9f
  0x2f  0x9f    0x9f

Phase 3 content-read FULLY SILICON-CLOSED via Plan B v3.

Retracts: prior 'Plan B v1+v2+v3 silicon-refuted' verdict from
commits 47dbf38 / 5be1bab / f0c9574 / 7813eb2 (orchestrator) +
d9f6d24 / b4a3ab2 / 58a205d (neorv32_rot).  The 'all 0xff at every
address' observation was a VALIDATION LOGIC ERROR: all addresses
tested in Phase C/D/E/F captures (addr 0..0x10 + 0x100000) happen
to be in EPCS-blank regions where the real flash content IS 0xff.
The wrapper was returning correct content all along.

Info 17011 'WYSIWYG SPI primitive converted to equivalent logic' is
BENIGN — normal Quartus synthesis note for asmiblock cells, does
NOT indicate broken silicon pin routing.  Pin map fit.rpt H1/D2/C1/H2
→ u_asmi~ALTERA_DCLK/SCE/SDO/DATA0 is the load-bearing evidence;
that was correct in v1+v2+v3 and silicon-confirmed now.

Bitstream md5 85e21f659c0fb5613b1d738e3808e1c6 (same wb_altasmi_parallel
RTL as v3, only firmware changed).  Stage2 ELF 18564 B (was 18568,
slight delta from reading 16 addrs vs 4 in loop).  Capture
docs/captures/diag_phase3_planB_v3_silicon_OK_addr20.log.
---
 sw/stage2_loader/main.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/main.c b/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
index ce495d2..3a9587d 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/main.c
@@ -766,10 +766,16 @@ static void mode_epcs_probe(void)
      *     the megafunction streams during firmware's MMIO setup overhead
      *     for steps 4-6
      * ================================================================= */
-    uart_puts("[P] --- Phase E: NH15 one-byte-per-op @0 ---\r\n");
-
-    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < 4u; i++) {
-        uint32_t a = i;
+    /* Plan B reverify 2026-05-18: read addr 0x20..0x2F instead of 0..3.
+     * EPCS dump revealed flash bytes 0..0x1F are all 0xff (factory ALINX
+     * bitstream header padding) — so prior "Plan B all 0xff" runs could
+     * not distinguish (a) wrapper-silicon-broken from (b) wrapper-OK
+     * reading real blank bytes.  At 0x20+ the bitstream has real content
+     * (dump byte 0x20 = 0x56 0xef 0xef 0xef ...), so this distinguishes. */
+    uart_puts("[P] --- Phase E: Plan B reverify @0x20 ---\r\n");
+
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < 16u; i++) {
+        uint32_t a = 0x20u + i;
 
         /* Step 1: reset + delay (NH13 stretcher = 16 sysclk; 32 sw_iters
          * is comfortably more than that). */
